WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.350
Peatlands cover only about 3 to
4 per cent of the world's land.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.870
Yet they hold twice the amount of
carbon found in the world's forests.

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.730
About 12 per cent of them are
already drained and degraded.

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.770
And carbon released anywhere mixes
through the whole atmosphere.

5
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.510
So can the whole world agree
to protect its forests,

6
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.990
bogs and farm soils?

7
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.330
Or will only rich countries act?

8
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.510
In this mission, you'll
test global strategies:

9
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.750
planting forests, restoring wetlands,
and farming to keep carbon in the soil.

10
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.470
Then you'll see how agreements and
carbon markets try to cut emissions,

11
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.930
and judge whether they can work.

12
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.960
Your mission: judge whether the whole world
can agree to protect its carbon stores.
